hadiths[30]{hadithnumber,text}:
"69001","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the people of knowledge did not disapprove of people fasting using tooth-sticks at any hour of the day in Ramadan"
"69002","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that the people of knowledge did not disapprove of people fasting using tooth-sticks at any hour of the day in Ramadan"
"69101","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman that when A'isha was doing itikaf she would only ask after sick people if she was walking and not if she was standing still. Malik said"
"69102","Yahya related to me from Malik from Ibn Shihab from Amra bint Abd ar-Rahman that when A'isha was doing itikaf she would only ask after sick people if she was walking and not if she was standing still. Malik said"
"69201","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had asked Ibn Shihab whether someone doing itikaf could go into a house to relieve himself"
"69202","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had asked Ibn Shihab whether someone doing itikaf could go into a house to relieve himself"
"69301","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Nafi"
"69302","Yahya related to me from Malik that he had heard that al-Qasim ibn Muhammad and Nafi"
"69401","[694] And he told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib ibn Yazid, that he said: I was a boy working with Abdullah Ibn Utbah Ibn Masoud was in the market of Medina during the time of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab. We used to take from the Nabataean ashram a mat for Imam Malik, Hadith: 694 Arabic Hadith:"
"69402","[694] And he told me on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib ibn Yazid, that he said: I was a boy working with Abdullah Ibn Utbah Ibn Masoud was in the market of Medina during the time of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab. We used to take from the Nabataean ashram a mat for Imam Malik, Hadith: 694 Arabic Hadith:"
"69501","[695] He told me on the authority of Malik that he asked Ibn Shihab on what basis he took Umar ibn al-Khattab from the Nabataean tribe, Ibn Shihab said: This was taken from them during the pre-Islamic era, so Omar obligated them to do so. Muwatta Imam Malik Hadith: 695 Arabic Hadith:"
"69502","[695] He told me on the authority of Malik that he asked Ibn Shihab on what basis he took Umar ibn al-Khattab from the Nabataean tribe, Ibn Shihab said: This was taken from them during the pre-Islamic era, so Omar obligated them to do so. Muwatta Imam Malik Hadith: 695 Arabic Hadith:"
"69601","Malik was asked whether someone who went into a mosque to do itikaf for the last ten days of Ramadan and stayed there for a day or two but then became ill and left the mosque"
"69602","Malik was asked whether someone who went into a mosque to do itikaf for the last ten days of Ramadan and stayed there for a day or two but then became ill and left the mosque"
"69701","Malik said: And it has reached me from Sulayman ibn Yasar the like of that. Malik said: Whoever dies and has upon him a vow (nadhr) of freeing a slave, or fasting, or charity, or a sacrificial camel (badanah), and he bequeaths that it be fulfilled from his wealth, then the charity and the badanah are in the third of his estate, and they take precedence over other bequests, except what is like them. That is because the obligatory vows and the like are not of the same nature as what one volunteers of that which is not obligatory. Rather, that is placed specifically in his third, not from the capital of his wealth, because if it were permissible for him to do that from his capital, the deceased would delay such obligatory matters until death approached, and when the wealth became his heirs', he would designate such things which no claimant was demanding from him. If that were permissible for him, he would delay these things until at his death he would designate them, and it might encompass all his wealth. That is not for him."
"69702","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab carried a horse in the path of Allah, then he wanted to buy it back. He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said: ""Do not buy it, and do not return to your charity."""
"69801","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"69802","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that the Messenger of Allah"
"69901","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"69902","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah"
"70001","And he related to me from Malik, from Nafi', that Abdullah ibn Umar used to say: He fasts the missed days of Ramadan consecutively if he broke his fast due to illness or travel."
"70002","And he related to me from Malik, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Iyad ibn Abdullah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh al-'Amiri, that he heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri saying: We used to give the Zakat al-Fitr as one sa' of food, or one sa' of barley, or one sa' of dates, or one sa' of dried yogurt (aqit), or one sa' of raisins, and that was with the sa' of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace."
"70101","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil that 'Anas ibn Malik said"
"70102","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Humayd at-Tawil that 'Anas ibn Malik said"
"70201","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Nafi from Ibn 'Umar that some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah"
"70202","Ziyad related to me from Malik from Nafi from Ibn 'Umar that some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah"
"70301","Ziyad related to me from Malik that he had heard a man he trusted of the people of knowledge say"
"70302","Ziyad related to me from Malik that he had heard a man he trusted of the people of knowledge say"
"70401","Ziyad related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab used to say"
"70402","Ziyad related to me from Malik that he had heard that Said ibn al-Musayyab used to say"
